{"id": "EUVD-2026-61078", "enisaUuid": "bc5ae2b8-1f4a-3815-9dd4-1148b2ba6233", "description": "A flaw was found in the submariner-operator component. The `submariner-k8s-broker-cluster` Role, which is assigned to joined clusters, possesses excessive permissions. This allows a compromised cluster to alter network configurations, specifically by overwriting other clusters' endpoint information. Consequently, an attacker can redirect inter-cluster tunnel traffic, enabling a Man-in-the-Middle (MITM) attack across the entire cluster mesh.", "datePublished": "2026-08-18T17:32:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T17:01:55", "baseScore": 6.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:63016", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:67538", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:67539", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:67540", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:67541", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:67542", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:67543", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:72880", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:85227", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-66780", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2507524"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-66780", "GHSA-3xmh-phwc-5f4g"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.58, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "07ebf41b-38d6-3ad6-a286-34379b0bb33e", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Advanced Cluster Management for Kubernetes 2.17", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1788073481"}, {"id": "1125a099-4a6d-38de-901d-a62bd1ad7736", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Advanced Cluster Management for Kubernetes 2.11", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1789135606"}, {"id": "2c3158b0-0c22-300b-82df-b5e3c8b33f7f", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Advanced Cluster Management for Kubernetes 2.17", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "produc